# .dockerignore — kept in sync with the concerns .gitignore already documents,
# plus Docker-specific ones.
#
# Real secrets: NEVER let these into a build context. A `COPY . .` with no
# exclusion bakes the live Mongo URI and JWT secret into an image layer —
# recoverable by anyone who can pull that image, long after the file is
# "deleted" from a later commit. Secrets reach the running container only via
# the platform's own env-var mechanism at deploy time, never via COPY.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

**/.git
**/.DS_Store

# Rebuilt inside their own build stages — never pulled in from the host, so a
# stale local `dist/` or `node_modules/` on the machine running `docker build`
# can't leak into the image or shadow what that stage produces itself.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
backend_api/__pycache__/
backend_api/**/__pycache__/
backend_api/.pytest_cache/

# Regenerated by the model-build stage (see Dockerfile) — never copied in from
# the host, so the image's model is always the one the pipeline just trained,
# not a stale local run.
backend_api/data/
backend_api/models_store/

# Real user data / large local artifacts — never belong in an image.
backups/
backend_api/backups/
*.bson

docs/
*.md
